@* MainLayoutSider — Auth project variant. Authentication module IS installed, so CascadingAuthenticationState
   is registered app-wide and AuthorizeView is safe to use. Only items whose context carries an
   authorization requirement get wrapped — everything else stays a plain, unwrapped MudNavLink.

   This mirrors the exact context example this skill was written against:
   - "a navigation link to the product list page with route '/product-list'" -> no requirement -> plain link
   - "a navigation link to the order list page with route '/order-list' which requires roles
      'Admin' or 'Write'" -> Roles-gated -> wrapped in AuthorizeView, Authorized-only, no NotAuthorized
      fragment (the item simply doesn't render for a user who doesn't qualify).

   The outer <nav class="ux-nav-drawer"> wrapper is the current scaffold's shape — there is no
   MudDrawer/DrawerOpen/DrawerOpenChanged binding here (an older scaffold generation used one;
   it no longer exists in MainLayout.razor or the code-behind, so don't reintroduce it). *@

<nav class="ux-nav-drawer">
    <MudNavMenu>
        <MudNavLink Href="/" Match="NavLinkMatch.All" Icon="@Icons.Material.Filled.Home">Home</MudNavLink>

        <MudNavLink Href="/product-list" Icon="@Icons.Material.Filled.Inventory2">Product List</MudNavLink>

        <AuthorizeView Roles="Admin,Write">
            <Authorized>
                <MudNavLink Href="/order-list" Icon="@Icons.Material.Filled.ListAlt">Order List</MudNavLink>
            </Authorized>
        </AuthorizeView>
    </MudNavMenu>
</nav>
